  "conclusions": {
    "wire": "250-byte schema5 base preserves schema4 layout and adds a separate232-byte type11 extension. Independent struct packing matches every byte of the136-byte record for7 native cases; both full SHA256 MACs and the full32-byte base-MAC binding verify. U64 record fields remain exact decimal strings.",
    "legacy": "417 schemas1..4 raw packet captures and independently signed packet hashes are identical to the pre-change frozen baseline; all4 legacy required-flex suppression gates hold.",
    "assembly": "Two pending sequences and a fixed first-fragment250ms lifetime. Duplicate parts do not extend it. Capacity eviction, expiry, malformed authenticated conflicts and other authenticated semantic errors retire sequences without changing completed ACK/liveness state. No partial public observation or ACK.",
    "age": "Raw age retains the original completed-sample timestamp, is bounded against the original producer stale limit, includes fragment wait/transit/drift/local elapsed, preserves first-pair and repeated/query lower bounds, and never turns an unknown age into freshness. Raw startup timestamp0 remains unknown; qualified scalarSource3 epoch0 stays valid. Clock reversal across all time-bearing receiver APIs latches a query requirement.",
    "sender": "Actual peer-slot/handler functions run in the native API model. A pending pair retains immutable bytes and original time across snapshot changes and SDK failures. Only both SDK-accepted parts enter the ACK window. Current time is checked immediately before every pair submission. Capability/query/unpair/key-context reset cancel old state; sequence exhaustion does not wrap.",
    "ack_health_and_led": "Complete fault observations can ACK link receipt while flex control remains blocked. Sensor ACKs cannot mask missing complete-engine ACKs. Required invalid/unknown/future/stale flex faults apply at zero RPM and are re-evaluated while a snapshot is held. Fault policy takes priority over pairing. Browser helpers distinguish link ACK from complete-engine ACK and reject malformed tuples.",
    "causal_capture": "Independently compiled actual sender capture reaches the frozen receiver in either arrival order. Both produce exact sender-handler ACK bytes at packet sequence9007199254741084; original raw age30ms stays30ms and conservative completion age is96ms. Flex qualification expires while base ADC/control freshness remains true."
  },
